title: Speed-Dependent Headlamp Lighting (Town & Highway Beam Shaping)
raw_community_title: Speed-Dependent Lighting (SDL)
category: Lighting
platform: F-150 Lightning
model_years: 2022-2026
trim: Lariat / Platinum / Flash (Matrix LED Headlamps)
source_sheet: Euro Kuga Mk3.5 / Ranger 6G / Mach-E GT Matrix LED Comparison & Livnitup
  Master Database
status: untested
notes: 'UNTESTED / EXPERIMENTAL: Enables Speed-Dependent Light Mode (m2_SDL_Enable)
  in the Headlamp Control

  Module (HCM). Automatically widens and softens the low-beam light distribution at
  lower city/town speeds

  to better illuminate curbs, ditches, and pedestrians, and narrows/focuses the beam
  further down the road

  at highway speeds. Uses existing vehicle speed data on the CAN bus and does not
  require suspension ride-height sensors.


  NOTE ON HCM CHECKSUMS: All HCM edits must be written as exact nibble values (never
  relative offsets). Because the HCM uses a secondary calibration CRC at 734-11-01,
  an external checksum calculator is required — reach out to Firn on the F-150 Lightning
  Forum or 14th Gen F-150 Forum to discuss.'
steps:
- module: HCM
  address: 734-05-01
  notes: 'Set to exact nibble value 1 (SDLE Enable). An external HCM checksum calculator
    is required for 734-11-01 — reach out to Firn on the F-150 Lightning Forum or
    14th Gen F-150 Forum to discuss.'
  targets:
  - mask: xxx* xxxx xx--
    community_hex: '1'
    type: discrete
    # Bit positions preserved for future AsBuiltPro HCM CRC calculator support:
    # bits:
    # - bit: 0
    #   action: 1
    #   feature_name: m2_SDL_Enable (SDLE)
    #   target_state: SDLE Enable
recipe_version: '1.1'
